  "findings": [
    "One118-segment history retirement encoded for1,979,298us and reserved the physical publication lane until1,979,332us; the34us difference includes reacquisition and observer overhead.",
    "The long interval is outside the authority mutex, but async_publication_in_flight blocks competing physical publications and defers rotation.",
    "The other original workload run recorded zero history compactions and still failed its one-second scheduled stream gate. History compaction is therefore not necessary for the observed stream failure.",
    "A retirement iteration is bounded in resident source memory, but currently captures every surplus history segment in one publication reservation; this measurement makes bounded scheduler retirement slices worth testing."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Two instrumented observations are not a performance-admission comparison, effect estimate, or statistical confidence interval.",
    "No causal overlap between a specific request wait and a history reservation was captured.",
    "Historical one-request-profile sample and rejected split-worker ABBA have different observer/work schedules; do not combine their durations as one trace.",
    "The runner inherited an inaccurate uninstrumented description in scope.json; actual requestProfile enabled/sampleEvery32 and diagnostic source are recorded here.",
    "No raw user payload or IDs were added to diagnostic records.",
    "No full-suite, broadSQLite, embedded,64KiB or realSIGKILL claim for this private observer build."
  ],
  "next": "Prototype scheduler-only retirement batches using existing launch-derived checkpoint materialization budget while preserving explicit operator semantics, current source verification, root fences and crash recovery; separately pursue the remaining foreground stream bottleneck."
